/*
 * Endpoint Name: RegisterEndpoint
 * HTTP Method: POST
 * Backend Route: /api/auth/register
 * 
 * Future Request Contract: RegisterRequest
 *   - FullName: string (required, max 100 chars)
 *   - Email: string (required, valid email, unique)
 *   - Password: string (required, min 6 chars, complexity rules)
 *   - ConfirmPassword: string (must match Password)
 * 
 * Future Response Contract: RegisterResponse
 *   - User: UserDto (newly created user profile)
 *   - Message: string (success message)
 * 
 * Required Permission: None (public endpoint)
 * 
 * Related Domain Entities:
 *   - User (Domain/Entities/User.cs)
 * 
 * Validation Steps:
 *   1. Validate FullName not empty, max 100 chars
 *   2. Validate Email format and uniqueness
 *   3. Validate Password min 6 chars, complexity rules
 *   4. Validate ConfirmPassword matches Password
 *   5. Check Email does not already exist in database
 * 
 * Implementation Steps:
 *   1. Receive RegisterRequest
 *   2. Check if Email already exists in AppDbContext
 *   3. Hash password using BCrypt.HashPassword()
 *   4. Create new User entity with hashed password
 *   5. Set default values: Status = Active, EmailConfirmed = false
 *   6. Save User to database
 *   7. Map User entity to UserDto (exclude PasswordHash)
 *   8. Return RegisterResponse with user info and success message
 * 
 * Error Cases:
 *   - 400 Bad Request: validation errors (invalid email, weak password, password mismatch)
 *   - 409 Conflict: email already exists
 *   - 500 Internal Server Error: unexpected database or hashing errors
 * 
 * EXPLICIT NOTE: NOT IMPLEMENTED IN PHASE 3C
 * This file is a TODO skeleton only. Real implementation will be done in later phase.
 */

